- **The revision pass earned the cap release.** The first grade capped Originality for ducking the Nazi-era record; the new closing paragraph of the shadow section (Bally's NZZ attack, the statute rewrite, the 1939 resignation, Scholem's "I slipped up" account) is sourced, both-columns, no-verdict, and type-free.
- **Citability check passed without the Evidence-6 cap.** The source audit flags 2 untagged quotes ("all the necessary data for the diagnosis" and the closing "classification of individuals means nothing") but both are attributed within their own paragraphs (Freeman/BBC 1959; Houston 1957 via *C.G. Jung Speaking*) — a proximity limitation of the script, not a sourcing hole. The one genuinely vague slot is the #shadowwork TikTok stat credited only to "per trade coverage"; the sidecar names it.
